  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Livelihood Response Programme in South Sudan (ELRP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FAO&apos;s quick intervention to provide time-critical livelihood support to 3.3 million crisis-affected, displaced and food - insecure people in South Sudan affected by the ongoing conflict. The programme is targeting vulnerable food insecure and displaced people, with a focus on those who have not been absorbed by host communities, and who have congregated in rural areas. Assistance will also be provided to host communities receiving the displaced.</narrative>
  </description>
